# Step 1 - Install Kafka (VM-4)

Download Kafka:

```bash
cd /opt

wget https://downloads.apache.org/kafka/3.9.1/kafka_2.13-3.9.1.tgz

tar -xzf kafka_2.13-3.9.1.tgz

mv kafka_2.13-3.9.1 kafka
```

---

# Step 2 - Configure Kafka

Edit:

```text
/opt/kafka/config/server.properties
```

Set:

```properties
broker.id=1

listeners=PLAINTEXT://0.0.0.0:9092

advertised.listeners=PLAINTEXT://<VM4-IP>:9092

log.dirs=/tmp/kafka-logs
```

If you're using Kafka in ZooKeeper mode (suitable for a POC), also set:

```properties
zookeeper.connect=<VM4-IP>:2181
```

---

# Step 3 - Start Kafka (VM-4)

Start the broker:

```bash
/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-server-start.sh \
/opt/kafka/config/server.properties
```

Verify:

```bash
netstat -an | grep 9092
```

---

# Step 4 - Create a Kafka Topic (VM-4)

Create a topic:

```bash
/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh \
--create \
--topic sales-topic \
--bootstrap-server localhost:9092 \
--partitions 1 \
--replication-factor 1
```

Verify:

```bash
/opt/kafka/bin/kafka-topics.sh \
--list \
--bootstrap-server localhost:9092
```

Expected:

```text
sales-topic
```

---

# Step 5 - Enable Kafka Extension (All Druid Nodes)

Because the ingestion task can run on any MiddleManager and Druid components need to understand Kafka ingestion specs, enable the Kafka extension on **VM-1, VM-2, and VM-3**.

Edit:

```text
/opt/druid/conf/druid/cluster/_common/common.runtime.properties
```

Update:

```properties
druid.extensions.loadList=[
"druid-kafka-indexing-service",
"druid-postgresql-metadata-storage"
]
```

If you're also keeping Azure ingestion available:

```properties
druid.extensions.loadList=[
"druid-kafka-indexing-service",
"druid-azure-extensions",
"druid-postgresql-metadata-storage"
]
```

Restart the Druid services after updating the configuration.

---

# Step 6 - Verify Kafka Connectivity (VM-3)

From the MiddleManager VM:

```bash
nc -vz <VM4-IP> 9092
```

Expected:

```text
Connection succeeded
```

