# What each VM does

| VM                                    | Responsibility                                                                                                                                             |
| ------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **VM-1 (Coordinator + Overlord)**     | Stores and manages the Kafka supervisor, schedules Kafka indexing tasks.                                                                                   |
| **VM-2 (Router + Broker)**            | Receives SQL queries and routes them to Historical nodes.                                                                                                  |
| **VM-3 (Historical + MiddleManager)** | MiddleManager consumes messages from Kafka, creates Druid segments, stores them in local deep storage. Historical loads those segments and serves queries. |
| **VM-4 (ZooKeeper + Kafka)**          | Hosts the Kafka broker (and ZooKeeper in this POC) and stores the Kafka topic and messages.                                                                |

## End-to-end flow

```text
Application
     │
     ▼
Kafka Topic (VM-4)
     │
     ▼
Overlord Supervisor (VM-1)
     │
     ▼
MiddleManager (VM-3)
     │
Consumes JSON messages
     │
Creates Druid segments
     │
Stores segments locally
     │
Historical loads segments
     │
Broker executes SQL
     │
Router returns results
```

### One note about Kafka versions

Current Kafka releases support both **KRaft mode** (without ZooKeeper) and **ZooKeeper mode** (legacy). Since your Druid cluster already includes a ZooKeeper VM, using Kafka in ZooKeeper mode is a straightforward choice for a POC. If you plan to build a production deployment on recent Kafka versions, I recommend using **KRaft mode** instead, as that's the direction Kafka is moving.



